<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ajwad ibn Zamil</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1507</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ajwad ibn Zamil was the greatest ruler of the Jabrid dynasty of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> in the late 15th century. From al-Ahsa he controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qatif">Qatif</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a> islands, extended his influence towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> and made a celebrated pilgrimage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> with a large retinue. His successors lost Bahrain and the coast to the Portuguese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p></div>
